# Capture census for bootstrap.bundle.js.
#
# 219 of bootstrap's 1,023 capture operands are the importer's `undefined`
# placeholder carrying an `enclosing_indices` entry (see CTJS/IR/Ops/Bindings.td
# and lib/CTJS/Import/Bytecode/Instructions.cpp, which still quote the older
# total of 1,021). tools/check/capture-census.py counts both over the module
# the importer writes. --expect-indexed is an exact count, so a change that
# stops writing the attribute and one that writes it where a real binding sits
# are both caught. Only the importer runs: no lowering and no
# --mlir-print-debuginfo, because the census counts operands and attributes
# and location suffixes would only lengthen the textual parse.
#
#
# RUN: ctjs-translate --ctbrowser-js-to-ctjs %{monorepo}/ctbrowser/vendor/bootstrap/bootstrap.bundle.js -o %t.mlir
# RUN: python3 %{monorepo}/tools/check/capture-census.py --expect-indexed 219 --expect-operands 1023 %t.mlir
